---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Pricing — rowlab"
  description="rowlab is free to run yourself. Hosted: Free with your own model key, Pro and Team coming soon."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Pricing</h1>
    <p>
      Running it yourself is free, forever: it's open source. The hosted version at
      <a href="https://app.rowlab.dev">app.rowlab.dev</a> is free with your own model key.
    </p>
  </div>

  <table class="plans">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th></th>
        <th>Free <span class="price">$0</span></th>
        <th>Pro <span class="soon">coming soon</span><span class="price">$20 / month</span></th>
        <th>Team <span class="soon">coming soon</span><span class="price">$20 / seat / month</span></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Model keys</td>
        <td>Your own OpenRouter key</td>
        <td>Your own key, or credits</td>
        <td>Your own key, or credits</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Answers a month</td>
        <td>50,000</td>
        <td>2 million</td>
        <td>5 million per seat</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Storage</td>
        <td>2 GB</td>
        <td>25 GB</td>
        <td>100 GB</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="lead">
    An answer is one model call for one row. The same prompt, model and row is never paid for twice.
    Credits, when they come, cost the provider's price plus 25%.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Self-hosted</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      <code>uvx rowlab</code> on a laptop, or Postgres, S3 and sign-in with WorkOS on your own servers.
      No limits beyond your hardware, no telemetry. The
      <a href="https://docs.rowlab.dev/self-host">self-hosting guide</a> has the details.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
